{
  "_comment": [
    "SITE-WIDE ORGANIZATION ENTITY — emit ONCE, on the homepage or /about only.",
    "",
    "Every other page in the encyclopedia references this node by @id and emits",
    "nothing further:  \"publisher\": { \"@id\": \"https://opengrants.io/#organization\" }",
    "Duplicating the full definition across 75 article pages creates 75 competing",
    "assertions of the same entity, which is the opposite of what entity markup is for.",
    "",
    "PLACEHOLDERS — a human must fill or delete each one. Do NOT guess a value.",
    "  {{LEGAL_NAME}}        registered legal entity name, exactly as filed",
    "  {{LOGO_URL}}          absolute URL to the logo image, minimum 112x112px",
    "  {{LOGO_WIDTH}}        integer pixels",
    "  {{LOGO_HEIGHT}}       integer pixels",
    "  {{FOUNDING_DATE}}     ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD)",
    "  {{STREET_ADDRESS}}    business address; omit the whole address node if remote",
    "  {{CITY}} {{REGION}} {{POSTAL_CODE}} {{COUNTRY}}   ISO 3166 country code",
    "  {{CONTACT_EMAIL}}     a monitored address",
    "  {{CRUNCHBASE_URL}}    optional additional sameAs; delete the line if unused",
    "",
    "VERIFIED VALUES — these are confirmed and should not be changed casually:",
    "  name, url, description, and the four sameAs profiles below are taken from",
    "  opengrants.io itself. Everything else is a placeholder on purpose.",
    "",
    "DELETE any property you cannot verify. An omitted property is neutral.",
    "A wrong one is a trust defect in a YMYL corpus, and every schema value must",
    "also appear in the visible text of the page that emits it.",
    "Google's recommended property set:",
    "https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/organization"
  ],
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#organization",
      "name": "OpenGrants",
      "legalName": "{{LEGAL_NAME}}",
      "url": "https://opengrants.io",
      "description": "OpenGrants connects organizations to grant funding and grant funding strategists.",
      "logo": {
        "@type": "ImageObject",
        "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#logo",
        "url": "{{LOGO_URL}}",
        "width": "{{LOGO_WIDTH}}",
        "height": "{{LOGO_HEIGHT}}",
        "caption": "OpenGrants"
      },
      "image": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#logo" },
      "foundingDate": "{{FOUNDING_DATE}}",
      "address": {
        "@type": "PostalAddress",
        "streetAddress": "{{STREET_ADDRESS}}",
        "addressLocality": "{{CITY}}",
        "addressRegion": "{{REGION}}",
        "postalCode": "{{POSTAL_CODE}}",
        "addressCountry": "{{COUNTRY}}"
      },
      "contactPoint": {
        "@type": "ContactPoint",
        "contactType": "customer support",
        "email": "{{CONTACT_EMAIL}}",
        "url": "https://opengrants.io"
      },
      "sameAs": [
        "https://www.linkedin.com/company/18966243/",
        "https://twitter.com/opengrants_io",
        "https://www.youtube.com/c/OpenGrants",
        "https://www.facebook.com/opengrants.io/",
        "{{CRUNCHBASE_URL}}"
      ],
      "publishingPrinciples": "https://opengrants.io/editorial-policy/",
      "correctionsPolicy": "https://opengrants.io/corrections/",
      "knowsAbout": [
        "Grant funding",
        "Federal grants",
        "Grant writing",
        "Nonprofit funding",
        "SBIR and STTR programs",
        "Grant compliance and award management"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#website",
      "url": "https://opengrants.io",
      "name": "OpenGrants",
      "publisher": { "@id": "https://opengrants.io/#organization" },
      "inLanguage": "en-US"
    }
  ]
}
